Dependencies are installed separately, not bundled in this distribution:
- lxml 6.1.3: BSD-3-Clause; its upstream LICENSES.txt lists additional terms
  for bundled resources and binary dependencies. https://lxml.de/
- mido 1.3.3: MIT. https://github.com/mido/mido
- packaging 26.3: Apache-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause. https://github.com/pypa/packaging
- pypdf 6.19.0: BSD-3-Clause. https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf

MuseScore, Poppler and optional FFmpeg are separate tools. MuseScore is GPLv3;
no tool executable or source-code dependency is bundled. Runtime MusicXML schemas
are fetched from their declared upstream URLs and are not bundled.

The source distribution includes our own public-domain October transcription,
arrangements and renders, with source/rights metadata under examples/tchaikovsky-october/.
The underlying Schirmer/Oesterle 1909 notation has a documented US public-domain basis.
Source scans, including the 1948 scan, are excluded. The example PDFs embed Edwin
and Leland under SIL OFL 1.1; complete notices are included in that example's licenses/.
No standalone font binaries are distributed. The portable skill ZIP contains no scores.
Private repository history, private acceptance logs and unrelated inputs are excluded.

